# Everything else: see .env.advanced.example — you almost certainly don't need it.
#
# GLM-5.3-Flash on four CMP 170HX cards. ./start.sh copies this file to .env on
# first run and reads only .env. Every setting is commented out and shows its
# default; uncomment a line to change it, then run ./start.sh restart.
# One KEY=value per line; a value on the command line beats .env for that run:
#   LAYOUT=pp4 ./start.sh restart

# tp4 = tensor-parallel 4 (fastest answer, x16 links); pp4 = pipeline-parallel 4 (x4 links, many users, long prompts).
# LAYOUT=tp4

# Listen address: 127.0.0.1 = this machine only; 0.0.0.0 = every interface (set API_KEY first).
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# API port.
# PORT=8000

# When set, every /v1 request must send "Authorization: Bearer <key>"; unset = no key.
# API_KEY=

# The model id clients send.
# SERVED_MODEL_NAME=glm-5.3-flash

# Where the checkpoints go, as an absolute path. Default: models/ in this repo.
# MODELS_DIR=/path/to/models

# container, or native (engine built in ./venv, for developers). Unset: native only if this checkout already has a native install.
# RUNTIME=container

# PCIe peer-to-peer all-reduce under tp4: 1 only if `nvidia-smi topo -p2p r` says OK for every pair (docs/how-to-use.md).
# VLLM_ALLOW_PCIE_P2P_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE=0
